* err.cir -- err1/err2/error(l1/l2/infnorm) coverage.
*
* RAMP(t)=2t, REF(t)=t: RAMP is always exactly twice REF for t>0, so every err1/err2 term
* (M-C)/max(minval,|M|) = (2t-t)/2t = 0.5 exactly; err2 (the mean) = 0.5, err1 (the RMS of the
* same terms) = sqrt(mean(0.5^2)) = 0.5 too -- by hand, matching gs-waveform-measurements' own
* err1_err2_hand_computed test (measured always exactly double comparison => both metrics 0.5).
*
* MEASURED_OFFSET(t) = REF(t) + 3 = t+3: a constant +3 offset from REF at every instant, so
* error_norm's L1 (mean |diff|), L2 (RMS diff), and InfNorm (max |diff|) all equal exactly 3 --
* a constant-offset difference makes all three norms coincide, by hand.
RAMP kind=pwl points=[[0,0],[10,20]]
REF kind=pwl points=[[0,0],[10,10]]
CONST3 kind=const value=3
MEASURED_OFFSET kind=sum inputs=REF,CONST3 signs=1,1
VA a 0 RAMPV
RAMPV kind=sig2voltage in=RAMP
R1 a 0 1000
VB b 0 REFV
REFV kind=sig2voltage in=REF
R2 b 0 1000
VC c 0 OFFV
OFFV kind=sig2voltage in=MEASURED_OFFSET
R3 c 0 1000

MEAS_ERR1 kind=measure type=err1 out=V(a) ref=V(b)
MEAS_ERR2 kind=measure type=err2 out=V(a) ref=V(b)
MEAS_L1 kind=measure type=error out=V(c) ref=V(b) norm=l1
MEAS_L2 kind=measure type=error out=V(c) ref=V(b) norm=l2
MEAS_INF kind=measure type=error out=V(c) ref=V(b) norm=infnorm
